<section id="S3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.2 </span>Proof of <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma 3.3. ‣ 3.1 The dual set 𝒮_𝑑 and log-convexity ‣ 3 Semiproper colourings ‣ Lower bounds for multivariate independence polynomials and their generalisations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a></h3>

<div id="S3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To sketch our proof of <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma 3.3. ‣ 3.1 The dual set 𝒮_𝑑 and log-convexity ‣ 3 Semiproper colourings ‣ Lower bounds for multivariate independence polynomials and their generalisations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a>, first recall that <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma 3.1. ‣ 3.1 The dual set 𝒮_𝑑 and log-convexity ‣ 3 Semiproper colourings ‣ Lower bounds for multivariate independence polynomials and their generalisations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a> showed that <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{d+1}(x,y)^{\frac{1}{d+1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{d+1}(x,y)^{\frac{1}{d+1}}</annotation></semantics></math> is concave on <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathbb{R}_{\geq 0})^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathbb{R}_{\geq 0})^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, so its tangent plane always lies above the surface <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z=A_{d+1}(x,y)^{\frac{1}{d+1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z=A_{d+1}(x,y)^{\frac{1}{d+1}}</annotation></semantics></math>. In other words, the boundary of <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> consists of those <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(a_{0},a_{1},a_{2})\in(\mathbb{R}_{\geq 0})^{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(a_{0},a_{1},a_{2})\in(\mathbb{R}_{\geq 0})^{3}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z=a_{0}+a_{1}x+a_{2}y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z=a_{0}+a_{1}x+a_{2}y</annotation></semantics></math> is tangent to <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z=A_{d+1}(x,y)^{\frac{1}{d+1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z=A_{d+1}(x,y)^{\frac{1}{d+1}}</annotation></semantics></math> at a point in the nonnegative quadrant. Thus, to show whether a point <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(v_{0},v_{1},v_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(v_{0},v_{1},v_{2})</annotation></semantics></math> is in <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}_{\Delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}_{\Delta}</annotation></semantics></math>, it is convenient to compute (or at least estimate) the value <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{0}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{0}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(v_{0}^{*},v_{1},v_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(v_{0}^{*},v_{1},v_{2})</annotation></semantics></math> lies on the boundary of <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}_{\Delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}_{\Delta}</annotation></semantics></math>, and check if <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{0}\geq v_{0}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>≥</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{0}\geq v_{0}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>.
It turns out that <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{0}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{0}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> essentially depends on the product <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{1}v_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{1}v_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>; see <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem5" title="Lemma 3.5. ‣ 3.2 Proof of ‣ 3 Semiproper colourings ‣ Lower bounds for multivariate independence polynomials and their generalisations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.5</span></a> for the precise statement. This allows us to reduce <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma 3.3. ‣ 3.1 The dual set 𝒮_𝑑 and log-convexity ‣ 3 Semiproper colourings ‣ Lower bounds for multivariate independence polynomials and their generalisations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a> to the case when <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda=\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda=\mu</annotation></semantics></math>.
After the reduction, proving a still technical but low-dimensional inequality concludes the proof.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{1},a_{2}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{1},a_{2}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, let</p>
<table id="S3.E7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi_{\Delta}(a_{1},a_{2})\coloneqq\inf\{a_{0}\geq 0:(a_{0},a_{1},a_{2})\in\mathcal{S}_{\Delta}\}=\sup_{x,y\geq 0}\bigl(A_{\Delta+1}(x,y)^{\frac{1}{\Delta+1}}-a_{1}x-a_{2}y\bigr)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">≔</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">inf</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi_{\Delta}(a_{1},a_{2})\coloneqq\inf\{a_{0}\geq 0:(a_{0},a_{1},a_{2})\in\mathcal{S}_{\Delta}\}=\sup_{x,y\geq 0}\bigl(A_{\Delta+1}(x,y)^{\frac{1}{\Delta+1}}-a_{1}x-a_{2}y\bigr).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3.7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Then for a given <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(w_{0},w_{1},w_{2})\in(\mathbb{R}_{&gt;0})^{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(w_{0},w_{1},w_{2})\in(\mathbb{R}_{&gt;0})^{3}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(w_{0},w_{1},w_{2})\in\mathcal{S}_{\Delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(w_{0},w_{1},w_{2})\in\mathcal{S}_{\Delta}</annotation></semantics></math> if and only if <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{0}\geq\Phi_{\Delta}(w_{1},w_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{0}\geq\Phi_{\Delta}(w_{1},w_{2})</annotation></semantics></math>. The following <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem5" title="Lemma 3.5. ‣ 3.2 Proof of ‣ 3 Semiproper colourings ‣ Lower bounds for multivariate independence polynomials and their generalisations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span></a> provides an upper bound for <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi_{\Delta}(a_{1},a_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi_{\Delta}(a_{1},a_{2})</annotation></semantics></math> which only depends on <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{1}a_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{1}a_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> up to a simple term.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 3.5</span></span><span id="S3.Thmtheorem5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmtheorem5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">There is a function <math id="S3.Thmtheorem5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Psi_{\Delta}\colon(0,1)\to\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Psi_{\Delta}\colon(0,1)\to\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> such that for all <math id="S3.Thmtheorem5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{1},a_{2}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{1},a_{2}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S3.Thmtheorem5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{1}a_{2}&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{1}a_{2}&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi_{\Delta}(a_{1},a_{2})\leq\Psi_{\Delta}(a_{1}a_{2})+(a_{1}+a_{2})/\Delta." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi_{\Delta}(a_{1},a_{2})\leq\Psi_{\Delta}(a_{1}a_{2})+(a_{1}+a_{2})/\Delta.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.Thmtheorem5.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem5.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Moreover, if <math id="S3.Thmtheorem5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{1}=a_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{1}=a_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, then equality holds.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S3.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">We want to identify the point <math id="S3.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x_{*},y_{*})\in\mathbb{R}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x_{*},y_{*})\in\mathbb{R}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> at which</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial_{x}\bigl(A_{\Delta+1}(x,y)^{\frac{1}{\Delta+1}}\bigr)=a_{1}\quad\text{and}\quad\partial_{y}\bigl(A_{\Delta+1}(x,y)^{\frac{1}{\Delta+1}}\bigr)=a_{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>x</mi></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext>and</mtext><mspace style="width:1.000em;" width="1.000em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>y</mi></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial_{x}\bigl(A_{\Delta+1}(x,y)^{\frac{1}{\Delta+1}}\bigr)=a_{1}\quad\text{and}\quad\partial_{y}\bigl(A_{\Delta+1}(x,y)^{\frac{1}{\Delta+1}}\bigr)=a_{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">Denote by <math id="S3.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi\coloneqq A_{\Delta+1}(x_{*},y_{*})^{\frac{1}{\Delta+1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi\coloneqq A_{\Delta+1}(x_{*},y_{*})^{\frac{1}{\Delta+1}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Since</span></p>
<table id="S3.EGx10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\partial_{x}\bigl(A_{\Delta+1}(x,y)^{\frac{1}{\Delta+1}}\bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>x</mi></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\partial_{x}\bigl(A_{\Delta+1}(x,y)^{\frac{1}{\Delta+1}}\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex29.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=(\Delta y+1)\,A_{\Delta+1}(x,y)^{-\Delta/(\Delta+1)}\quad\text{and}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mtext>and</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(\Delta y+1)\,A_{\Delta+1}(x,y)^{-\Delta/(\Delta+1)}\quad\text{and}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex30"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\partial_{y}\bigl(A_{\Delta+1}(x,y)^{\frac{1}{\Delta+1}}\bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>y</mi></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\partial_{y}\bigl(A_{\Delta+1}(x,y)^{\frac{1}{\Delta+1}}\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex30.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=(\Delta x+1)\,A_{\Delta+1}(x,y)^{-\Delta/(\Delta+1)}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(\Delta x+1)\,A_{\Delta+1}(x,y)^{-\Delta/(\Delta+1)},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><math id="S3.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{1}=(1+\Delta y_{*})\xi^{-\Delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ξ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{1}=(1+\Delta y_{*})\xi^{-\Delta}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS2.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text"> and <math id="S3.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{2}=(1+\Delta x_{*})\xi^{-\Delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ξ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{2}=(1+\Delta x_{*})\xi^{-\Delta}</annotation></semantics></math>. Using the identity <math id="S3.SS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\Delta+1)(\Delta x+1)(\Delta y+1)=\Delta A_{\Delta+1}(x,y)+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\Delta+1)(\Delta x+1)(\Delta y+1)=\Delta A_{\Delta+1}(x,y)+1</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="S3.SS2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ξ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi</annotation></semantics></math> is a zero of the polynomial <math id="S3.SS2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(X)\coloneqq(\Delta+1)a_{1}a_{2}X^{2\Delta}-\Delta X^{\Delta+1}-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(X)\coloneqq(\Delta+1)a_{1}a_{2}X^{2\Delta}-\Delta X^{\Delta+1}-1</annotation></semantics></math>.
The following claim, together with the assumption <math id="S3.SS2.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;a_{1}a_{2}&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;a_{1}a_{2}&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>, guarantees the existence of a unique zero.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem6" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_claim">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Claim 3.6</span></span><span id="S3.Thmtheorem6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmtheorem6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For <math id="S3.Thmtheorem6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;s&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;s&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.Thmtheorem6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(X)</annotation></semantics></math> has a unique zero <math id="S3.Thmtheorem6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi_{\Delta}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi_{\Delta}(s)</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="S3.Thmtheorem6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1,\infty)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1,\infty)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="S3.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_itemize">
</ul>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Note that <math id="S3.SS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(0)=-1&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(0)=-1&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.SS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(1)=(\Delta+1)(s-1)&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(1)=(\Delta+1)(s-1)&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S3.SS2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(X)\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(X)\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="S3.SS2.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math>.
In addition, <math id="S3.SS2.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{\prime}(X)=\Delta(\Delta+1)X^{\Delta}(2sX^{\Delta-1}-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{\prime}(X)=\Delta(\Delta+1)X^{\Delta}(2sX^{\Delta-1}-1)</annotation></semantics></math> has at most one positive zero <math id="S3.SS2.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\coloneqq(2s)^{-\frac{1}{\Delta-1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>≔</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\coloneqq(2s)^{-\frac{1}{\Delta-1}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Also, <math id="S3.SS2.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{\prime}(X)&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{\prime}(X)&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="S3.SS2.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(0,\alpha)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(0,\alpha)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS2.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{\prime}(X)&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{\prime}(X)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="S3.SS2.p5.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\alpha,\infty)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\alpha,\infty)</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, <math id="S3.SS2.p5.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> has a unique zero on <math id="S3.SS2.p5.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(0,\infty)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(0,\infty)</annotation></semantics></math>, which must be larger than <math id="S3.SS2.p5.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎To emphasise the dependence on <math id="S3.SS2.p5.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{1}a_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{1}a_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, write
<math id="S3.SS2.p5.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{\Delta+1}(x_{*},y_{*})^{\frac{1}{\Delta+1}}=\xi_{\Delta}(a_{1}a_{2})&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{\Delta+1}(x_{*},y_{*})^{\frac{1}{\Delta+1}}=\xi_{\Delta}(a_{1}a_{2})&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math>. This determines</span></p>
<table id="S3.EGx11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.E8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle x_{*}=\frac{a_{2}\xi_{\Delta}(a_{1}a_{2})^{\Delta}-1}{\Delta}\quad\text{and}\quad y_{*}=\frac{a_{1}\xi_{\Delta}(a_{1}a_{2})^{\Delta}-1}{\Delta}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext>and</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle x_{*}=\frac{a_{2}\xi_{\Delta}(a_{1}a_{2})^{\Delta}-1}{\Delta}\quad\text{and}\quad y_{*}=\frac{a_{1}\xi_{\Delta}(a_{1}a_{2})^{\Delta}-1}{\Delta}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3.8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">In general, this <math id="S3.SS2.p5.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x_{*},y_{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x_{*},y_{*})</annotation></semantics></math> need not lie in <math id="S3.SS2.p5.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathbb{R}_{\geq 0})^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathbb{R}_{\geq 0})^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. Instead, we consider a convex set containing <math id="S3.SS2.p5.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathbb{R}_{\geq 0})^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathbb{R}_{\geq 0})^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS2.p5.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x_{*},y_{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x_{*},y_{*})</annotation></semantics></math>; we claim <math id="S3.SS2.p5.m20" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Omega\coloneqq\{(x,y)\in\mathbb{R}^{2}:A_{\Delta+1}(x,y)&gt;0,\,y&gt;-1/\Delta\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo rspace="0em">&gt;</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega\coloneqq\{(x,y)\in\mathbb{R}^{2}:A_{\Delta+1}(x,y)&gt;0,\,y&gt;-1/\Delta\}</annotation></semantics></math> is suitable. That <math id="S3.SS2.p5.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathbb{R}_{\geq 0})^{2}\subseteq\Omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>⊆</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathbb{R}_{\geq 0})^{2}\subseteq\Omega</annotation></semantics></math> is clear, and <math id="S3.SS2.p5.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{\Delta+1}(x_{*},y_{*})=\xi_{\Delta}(a_{1}a_{2})^{\Delta+1}&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{\Delta+1}(x_{*},y_{*})=\xi_{\Delta}(a_{1}a_{2})^{\Delta+1}&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math>. In addition, <math id="S3.SS2.p5.m23" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="y_{*}&gt;-1/\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo rspace="0em">&gt;</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{*}&gt;-1/\Delta</annotation></semantics></math> follows from <math id="S3.SS2.p5.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi_{\Delta}(a_{1}a_{2})&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi_{\Delta}(a_{1}a_{2})&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS2.p5.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{1}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{1}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. To see that <math id="S3.SS2.p5.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega</annotation></semantics></math> is convex, let</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex31" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="g(y)\coloneqq-\frac{(\Delta+1)y+1}{(\Delta+1)(\Delta y+1)}\quad\text{so that}\quad\Omega=\{(x,y)\in\mathbb{R}^{2}:x&gt;g(y),\,y&gt;-1/\Delta\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">≔</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mtext>so that</mtext><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo rspace="0em">&gt;</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(y)\coloneqq-\frac{(\Delta+1)y+1}{(\Delta+1)(\Delta y+1)}\quad\text{so that}\quad\Omega=\{(x,y)\in\mathbb{R}^{2}:x&gt;g(y),\,y&gt;-1/\Delta\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p5.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p5.3.1" class="ltx_text">Then <math id="S3.SS2.p5.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g^{\prime\prime}(y)=2\Delta(\Delta+1)^{-1}(\Delta y+1)^{-3}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g^{\prime\prime}(y)=2\Delta(\Delta+1)^{-1}(\Delta y+1)^{-3}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="S3.SS2.p5.m28" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="y&gt;-1/\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo rspace="0em">&gt;</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y&gt;-1/\Delta</annotation></semantics></math>, so <math id="S3.SS2.p5.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> is convex on <math id="S3.SS2.p5.m30" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="(-1/\Delta,\infty)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(-1/\Delta,\infty)</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence, <math id="S3.SS2.p5.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega</annotation></semantics></math> is convex. Now by <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma 3.1. ‣ 3.1 The dual set 𝒮_𝑑 and log-convexity ‣ 3 Semiproper colourings ‣ Lower bounds for multivariate independence polynomials and their generalisations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>, <math id="S3.SS2.p5.m32" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{\Delta+1}(x,y)^{\frac{1}{\Delta+1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{\Delta+1}(x,y)^{\frac{1}{\Delta+1}}</annotation></semantics></math> is concave on <math id="S3.SS2.p5.m33" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega</annotation></semantics></math>, so</span></p>
<table id="S3.EGx12" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex32"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Phi_{\Delta}(a_{1},a_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Phi_{\Delta}(a_{1},a_{2})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex32.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\sup_{(x,y)\in\Omega}\bigl(A_{\Delta+1}(x,y)^{\frac{1}{\Delta+1}}-a_{1}x-a_{2}y\bigr)=A_{\Delta+1}(x_{*},y_{*})^{\frac{1}{\Delta+1}}-a_{1}x_{*}-a_{2}y_{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.1389em">≤</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\sup_{(x,y)\in\Omega}\bigl(A_{\Delta+1}(x,y)^{\frac{1}{\Delta+1}}-a_{1}x-a_{2}y\bigr)=A_{\Delta+1}(x_{*},y_{*})^{\frac{1}{\Delta+1}}-a_{1}x_{*}-a_{2}y_{*}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex33"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\xi_{\Delta}(a_{1}a_{2})-(2/\Delta)a_{1}a_{2}\xi_{\Delta}(a_{1}a_{2})^{\Delta}+(a_{1}+a_{2})/\Delta." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\xi_{\Delta}(a_{1}a_{2})-(2/\Delta)a_{1}a_{2}\xi_{\Delta}(a_{1}a_{2})^{\Delta}+(a_{1}+a_{2})/\Delta.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p5.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p5.4.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="S3.SS2.p5.m34" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Psi_{\Delta}(s)\coloneqq\xi_{\Delta}(s)-(2/\Delta)s\xi_{\Delta}(s)^{\Delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Psi_{\Delta}(s)\coloneqq\xi_{\Delta}(s)-(2/\Delta)s\xi_{\Delta}(s)^{\Delta}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S3.SS2.p5.m35" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;s&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;s&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math> so that <math id="S3.SS2.p5.m36" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi_{\Delta}(a_{1},a_{2})\leq\Psi_{\Delta}(a_{1}a_{2})+(a_{1}+a_{2})/\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi_{\Delta}(a_{1},a_{2})\leq\Psi_{\Delta}(a_{1}a_{2})+(a_{1}+a_{2})/\Delta</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">To see the ‘moreover’ part, suppose <math id="S3.SS2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{1}=a_{2}=\sqrt{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mi>s</mi></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{1}=a_{2}=\sqrt{s}</annotation></semantics></math> for some <math id="S3.SS2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. Then by definition of <math id="S3.SS2.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi_{\Delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi_{\Delta}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex34" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\Delta+1)s\xi_{\Delta}(s)^{2\Delta}=\Delta\xi_{\Delta}(s)^{\Delta+1}+1&gt;\Delta+1," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\Delta+1)s\xi_{\Delta}(s)^{2\Delta}=\Delta\xi_{\Delta}(s)^{\Delta+1}+1&gt;\Delta+1,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">so <math id="S3.SS2.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{1}\xi_{\Delta}(a_{1}a_{2})^{\Delta}=a_{2}\xi_{\Delta}(a_{1}a_{2})^{\Delta}&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msup></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{1}\xi_{\Delta}(a_{1}a_{2})^{\Delta}=a_{2}\xi_{\Delta}(a_{1}a_{2})^{\Delta}&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math>. Then <math id="S3.SS2.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{*}=y_{*}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{*}=y_{*}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> by (<a href="#S3.E8" title="Equation 3.8 ‣ Proof. ‣ 3.2 Proof of ‣ 3 Semiproper colourings ‣ Lower bounds for multivariate independence polynomials and their generalisations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.8</span></a>) and therefore,</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex35" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi_{\Delta}(a_{1},a_{2})=A_{\Delta+1}(x_{*},y_{*})^{\frac{1}{\Delta+1}}-a_{1}x_{*}-a_{2}y_{*}=\Psi_{\Delta}(a_{1}a_{2})+(a_{1}+a_{2})/\Delta.\qed" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">.</mo><mo class="ltx_mathvariant_italic" lspace="0.0835em" mathvariant="italic" separator="true">∎</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi_{\Delta}(a_{1},a_{2})=A_{\Delta+1}(x_{*},y_{*})^{\frac{1}{\Delta+1}}-a_{1}x_{*}-a_{2}y_{*}=\Psi_{\Delta}(a_{1}a_{2})+(a_{1}+a_{2})/\Delta.\qed</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p7.1" class="ltx_p">The following inequality will allow us to check that the condition <math id="S3.SS2.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{1}a_{2}&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{1}a_{2}&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math> in <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem5" title="Lemma 3.5. ‣ 3.2 Proof of ‣ 3 Semiproper colourings ‣ Lower bounds for multivariate independence polynomials and their generalisations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.5</span></a> holds in the proof of <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma 3.3. ‣ 3.1 The dual set 𝒮_𝑑 and log-convexity ‣ 3 Semiproper colourings ‣ Lower bounds for multivariate independence polynomials and their generalisations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem7" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 3.7</span></span><span id="S3.Thmtheorem7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmtheorem7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S3.Thmtheorem7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.Thmtheorem7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x,y\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x,y\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>. Then
<math id="S3.Thmtheorem7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(dx+1)^{d+1}(dy+1)^{d+1}\leq\bigl((d+1)dxy+(d+1)(x+y)+1\bigr)^{2d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(dx+1)^{d+1}(dy+1)^{d+1}\leq\bigl((d+1)dxy+(d+1)(x+y)+1\bigr)^{2d}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Equality holds if and only if <math id="S3.Thmtheorem7.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=y=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=y=0</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S3.SS2.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="S3.SS2.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\coloneqq x+y+dxy" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\coloneqq x+y+dxy</annotation></semantics></math>. Then the desired inequality is equivalent to <math id="S3.SS2.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(dt+1)^{d+1}\leq((d+1)t+1)^{2d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>≤</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(dt+1)^{d+1}\leq((d+1)t+1)^{2d}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let <math id="S3.SS2.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(t)\coloneqq 2d\log((d+1)t+1)-(d+1)\log(dt+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(t)\coloneqq 2d\log((d+1)t+1)-(d+1)\log(dt+1)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then <math id="S3.SS2.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(0)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(0)=0</annotation></semantics></math> and for <math id="S3.SS2.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex36" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{\prime}(t)=d(d+1)\frac{(d-1)t+1}{(dt+1)((d+1)t+1)}&gt;0.\qed" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">.</mo><mo class="ltx_mathvariant_italic" lspace="0.0835em" mathvariant="italic" separator="true">∎</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{\prime}(t)=d(d+1)\frac{(d-1)t+1}{(dt+1)((d+1)t+1)}&gt;0.\qed</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p9.1" class="ltx_p">Now we are ready to prove <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma 3.3. ‣ 3.1 The dual set 𝒮_𝑑 and log-convexity ‣ 3 Semiproper colourings ‣ Lower bounds for multivariate independence polynomials and their generalisations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma 3.3. ‣ 3.1 The dual set 𝒮_𝑑 and log-convexity ‣ 3 Semiproper colourings ‣ Lower bounds for multivariate independence polynomials and their generalisations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="S3.SS2.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">For brevity, let</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex37" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A\coloneqq A_{d}(\lambda,\mu),\qquad B\coloneqq B_{d}(\mu),\qquad C\coloneqq B_{d}(\lambda),\qquad D\coloneqq A_{d+1}(\lambda,\mu)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A\coloneqq A_{d}(\lambda,\mu),\qquad B\coloneqq B_{d}(\mu),\qquad C\coloneqq B_{d}(\lambda),\qquad D\coloneqq A_{d+1}(\lambda,\mu),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p10.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p10.2.1" class="ltx_text">and</span></p>
<table id="S3.E9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{0}\coloneqq A^{\frac{\Delta}{d}}D^{-\frac{\Delta}{d+1}},\qquad w_{1}\coloneqq B^{\frac{\Delta}{d}}D^{-\frac{\Delta}{d+1}},\qquad w_{2}\coloneqq C^{\frac{\Delta}{d}}D^{-\frac{\Delta}{d+1}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mfrac><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>d</mi></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msup><mi>B</mi><mfrac><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>d</mi></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mfrac><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>d</mi></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{0}\coloneqq A^{\frac{\Delta}{d}}D^{-\frac{\Delta}{d+1}},\qquad w_{1}\coloneqq B^{\frac{\Delta}{d}}D^{-\frac{\Delta}{d+1}},\qquad w_{2}\coloneqq C^{\frac{\Delta}{d}}D^{-\frac{\Delta}{d+1}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3.9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p10.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p10.3.1" class="ltx_text">Then the goal is to show that</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex38" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(w_{0},w_{1},w_{2})\in\mathcal{S}_{\Delta}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(w_{0},w_{1},w_{2})\in\mathcal{S}_{\Delta}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p10.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p10.4.1" class="ltx_text">Note that</span></p>
<table id="S3.E10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A=A(B,C)\coloneqq\frac{(d-1)BC+B+C-1}{d}\quad\text{and}\quad D=\frac{(d+1)BC-1}{d}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></mfrac></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext>and</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A=A(B,C)\coloneqq\frac{(d-1)BC+B+C-1}{d}\quad\text{and}\quad D=\frac{(d+1)BC-1}{d}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3.10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">We have <math id="S3.SS2.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{1}w_{2}\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{1}w_{2}\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math> since <math id="S3.SS2.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B^{d+1}C^{d+1}\leq D^{2d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B^{d+1}C^{d+1}\leq D^{2d}</annotation></semantics></math> by <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem7" title="Proposition 3.7. ‣ 3.2 Proof of ‣ 3 Semiproper colourings ‣ Lower bounds for multivariate independence polynomials and their generalisations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.7</span></a>. If <math id="S3.SS2.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{1}w_{2}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{1}w_{2}=1</annotation></semantics></math>, then equality holds in <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem7" title="Proposition 3.7. ‣ 3.2 Proof of ‣ 3 Semiproper colourings ‣ Lower bounds for multivariate independence polynomials and their generalisations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.7</span></a>, implying <math id="S3.SS2.p11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda=\mu=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda=\mu=0</annotation></semantics></math>. Then the goal reduces to checking <math id="S3.SS2.p11.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1,1,1)\in\mathcal{S}_{\Delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1,1,1)\in\mathcal{S}_{\Delta}</annotation></semantics></math>. This indeed holds since for all <math id="S3.SS2.p11.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x,y\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x,y\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S3.EGx13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex39"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(1+x+y)^{\Delta+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(1+x+y)^{\Delta+1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex39.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq\binom{\Delta+1}{2}(x+y)^{2}+(\Delta+1)(x+y)+1\geq(\Delta+1)\Delta xy+(\Delta+1)(x+y)+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq\binom{\Delta+1}{2}(x+y)^{2}+(\Delta+1)(x+y)+1\geq(\Delta+1)\Delta xy+(\Delta+1)(x+y)+1</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex40"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=A_{\Delta+1}(x,y)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=A_{\Delta+1}(x,y).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p12" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS2.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Reduction to the symmetric case.</span> In what follows, assume <math id="S3.SS2.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{1}w_{2}&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{1}w_{2}&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>. Our first step is to reduce it to the case <math id="S3.SS2.p12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda=\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda=\mu</annotation></semantics></math>.
Recall that <math id="S3.SS2.p12.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(w_{0},w_{1},w_{2})\in\mathcal{S}_{\Delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(w_{0},w_{1},w_{2})\in\mathcal{S}_{\Delta}</annotation></semantics></math> is equivalent to <math id="S3.SS2.p12.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{0}\geq\Phi_{\Delta}(w_{1},w_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{0}\geq\Phi_{\Delta}(w_{1},w_{2})</annotation></semantics></math>. By <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem5" title="Lemma 3.5. ‣ 3.2 Proof of ‣ 3 Semiproper colourings ‣ Lower bounds for multivariate independence polynomials and their generalisations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.5</span></a>,</p>
<table id="S3.Ex41" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{0}-\Phi_{\Delta}(w_{1},w_{2})\geq w_{0}-\frac{w_{1}+w_{2}}{\Delta}-\Psi_{\Delta}(w_{1}w_{2})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{0}-\Phi_{\Delta}(w_{1},w_{2})\geq w_{0}-\frac{w_{1}+w_{2}}{\Delta}-\Psi_{\Delta}(w_{1}w_{2}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p12.2" class="ltx_p">Consider <math id="S3.SS2.p12.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.SS2.p12.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S3.SS2.p12.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> as functions of <math id="S3.SS2.p12.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS2.p12.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>, which is possible due to (<a href="#S3.E9" title="Equation 3.9 ‣ Proof of . ‣ 3.2 Proof of ‣ 3 Semiproper colourings ‣ Lower bounds for multivariate independence polynomials and their generalisations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.9</span></a>) and (<a href="#S3.E10" title="Equation 3.10 ‣ Proof of . ‣ 3.2 Proof of ‣ 3 Semiproper colourings ‣ Lower bounds for multivariate independence polynomials and their generalisations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.10</span></a>). Note that <math id="S3.SS2.p12.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{1}w_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{1}w_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> is constant when <math id="S3.SS2.p12.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="BC" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">BC</annotation></semantics></math> is fixed, and hence, so is <math id="S3.SS2.p12.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Psi_{\Delta}(w_{1}w_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Psi_{\Delta}(w_{1}w_{2})</annotation></semantics></math>. We claim that if <math id="S3.SS2.p12.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="BC" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">BC</annotation></semantics></math> is fixed, then <math id="S3.SS2.p12.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{0}-(w_{1}+w_{2})/\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{0}-(w_{1}+w_{2})/\Delta</annotation></semantics></math> is minimized when <math id="S3.SS2.p12.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B=C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B=C</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S3.SS2.p12.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\coloneqq(BC)^{1/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>≔</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\coloneqq(BC)^{1/2}</annotation></semantics></math> and write <math id="S3.SS2.p12.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B=B(t)\coloneqq Ke^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B=B(t)\coloneqq Ke^{t}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS2.p12.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C=C(t)\coloneqq Ke^{-t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C=C(t)\coloneqq Ke^{-t}</annotation></semantics></math>. Without loss of generality, assume <math id="S3.SS2.p12.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B\geq C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B\geq C</annotation></semantics></math> so that <math id="S3.SS2.p12.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S3.SS2.p12.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\coloneqq\Delta/d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\coloneqq\Delta/d</annotation></semantics></math>. Then</p>
<table id="S3.Ex42" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{d}{dt}A(B,C)=\frac{B^{\prime}(t)+C^{\prime}(t)}{d}=\frac{B-C}{d}\quad\text{and}\quad\frac{d}{dt}(B^{p}+C^{p})=p(B^{p}-C^{p})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>B</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mi>d</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mi>d</mi></mfrac></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext>and</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>B</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mi>p</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>B</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mi>p</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{d}{dt}A(B,C)=\frac{B^{\prime}(t)+C^{\prime}(t)}{d}=\frac{B-C}{d}\quad\text{and}\quad\frac{d}{dt}(B^{p}+C^{p})=p(B^{p}-C^{p}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p12.3" class="ltx_p">By (<a href="#S3.E10" title="Equation 3.10 ‣ Proof of . ‣ 3.2 Proof of ‣ 3 Semiproper colourings ‣ Lower bounds for multivariate independence polynomials and their generalisations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.10</span></a>), <math id="S3.SS2.p12.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> is fixed and thus, by (<a href="#S3.E9" title="Equation 3.9 ‣ Proof of . ‣ 3.2 Proof of ‣ 3 Semiproper colourings ‣ Lower bounds for multivariate independence polynomials and their generalisations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.9</span></a>),</p>
<table id="S3.Ex43" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{d}{dt}(w_{0}-(w_{1}+w_{2})/\Delta)=d^{-1}\bigl(p(B-C)A^{p-1}-(B^{p}-C^{p})\bigr)D^{-\frac{\Delta}{d+1}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>B</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mi>p</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{d}{dt}(w_{0}-(w_{1}+w_{2})/\Delta)=d^{-1}\bigl(p(B-C)A^{p-1}-(B^{p}-C^{p})\bigr)D^{-\frac{\Delta}{d+1}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p12.4" class="ltx_p">This is nonnegative, since <math id="S3.SS2.p12.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A\geq B\geq C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A\geq B\geq C</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S3.SS2.p12.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A\geq B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A\geq B</annotation></semantics></math> follows from <math id="S3.SS2.p12.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, so that</p>
<table id="S3.Ex44" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(B-C)A^{p-1}=\int_{C}^{B}pA^{p-1}\mathop{}\!d\zeta\geq\int_{C}^{B}p\zeta^{p-1}\mathop{}\!d\zeta=B^{p}-C^{p}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>C</mi><mi>B</mi></msubsup><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>ζ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≥</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>C</mi><mi>B</mi></msubsup><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ζ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>ζ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>B</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mi>p</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(B-C)A^{p-1}=\int_{C}^{B}pA^{p-1}\mathop{}\!d\zeta\geq\int_{C}^{B}p\zeta^{p-1}\mathop{}\!d\zeta=B^{p}-C^{p}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p12.5" class="ltx_p">Thus, <math id="S3.SS2.p12.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{0}-(w_{1}+w_{2})/\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{0}-(w_{1}+w_{2})/\Delta</annotation></semantics></math> is minimized when <math id="S3.SS2.p12.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=0</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore,</p>
