<p id="S3.SS2.p12.6" class="ltx_p">Here the equality follows from the ‘moreover’ part of <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem5" title="Lemma 3.5. ‣ 3.2 Proof of ‣ 3 Semiproper colourings ‣ Lower bounds for multivariate independence polynomials and their generalisations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.5</span></a> with <math id="S3.SS2.p12.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{1}(K,K)=w_{2}(K,K)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{1}(K,K)=w_{2}(K,K)</annotation></semantics></math>. In addition, <math id="S3.SS2.p12.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{1}(B,C)w_{2}(B,C)=w_{1}(K,K)w_{2}(K,K)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{1}(B,C)w_{2}(B,C)=w_{1}(K,K)w_{2}(K,K)</annotation></semantics></math> since <math id="S3.SS2.p12.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{1}w_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{1}w_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> depends only on <math id="S3.SS2.p12.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="BC" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">BC</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS2.p12.m32" class="ltx_Math" alttext="BC=K^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">BC=K^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence, it suffices to consider the case <math id="S3.SS2.p12.m33" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B=C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B=C</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e., <math id="S3.SS2.p12.m34" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda=\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda=\mu</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p13" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS2.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Analysis of the symmetric case.</span> Let <math id="S3.SS2.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{d}(\lambda)\coloneqq A_{d}(\lambda,\lambda)=d(d-1)\lambda^{2}+2d\lambda+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{d}(\lambda)\coloneqq A_{d}(\lambda,\lambda)=d(d-1)\lambda^{2}+2d\lambda+1</annotation></semantics></math>.
Recall that the goal <math id="S3.SS2.p13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(w_{0},w_{1},w_{2})\in\mathcal{S}_{\Delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(w_{0},w_{1},w_{2})\in\mathcal{S}_{\Delta}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S3.SS2.p13.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda=\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda=\mu</annotation></semantics></math> states that for all integer <math id="S3.SS2.p13.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq d\leq\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq d\leq\Delta</annotation></semantics></math> and reals <math id="S3.SS2.p13.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS2.p13.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x,y\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x,y\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="S3.Ex48" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bigl(A_{d}(\lambda)^{\frac{\Delta}{d}}+(x+y)B_{d}(\lambda)^{\frac{\Delta}{d}}\bigr)A_{d+1}(\lambda)^{-\frac{\Delta}{d+1}}\geq A_{\Delta+1}(x,y)^{\frac{1}{\Delta+1}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>d</mi></mfrac></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>d</mi></mfrac></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigl(A_{d}(\lambda)^{\frac{\Delta}{d}}+(x+y)B_{d}(\lambda)^{\frac{\Delta}{d}}\bigr)A_{d+1}(\lambda)^{-\frac{\Delta}{d+1}}\geq A_{\Delta+1}(x,y)^{\frac{1}{\Delta+1}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p13.2" class="ltx_p">As was shown in (<a href="#S3.Ex16" title="In 3.1 The dual set 𝒮_𝑑 and log-convexity ‣ 3 Semiproper colourings ‣ Lower bounds for multivariate independence polynomials and their generalisations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.6</span></a>), if <math id="S3.SS2.p13.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=\Delta</annotation></semantics></math>, then the left-hand side corresponds to the tangent plane of <math id="S3.SS2.p13.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z=A_{\Delta+1}(x,y)^{\frac{1}{\Delta+1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z=A_{\Delta+1}(x,y)^{\frac{1}{\Delta+1}}</annotation></semantics></math> at <math id="S3.SS2.p13.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x,y)=(\lambda,\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x,y)=(\lambda,\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math> lying above the right-hand side, so the inequality holds.
Furthermore, if <math id="S3.SS2.p13.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x+y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x+y</annotation></semantics></math> is fixed, then <math id="S3.SS2.p13.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{\Delta+1}(x,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{\Delta+1}(x,y)</annotation></semantics></math>, an increasing function of <math id="S3.SS2.p13.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="xy" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">xy</annotation></semantics></math>, is maximized when <math id="S3.SS2.p13.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=y</annotation></semantics></math>. Assuming <math id="S3.SS2.p13.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=y</annotation></semantics></math>, it suffices to show that for any <math id="S3.SS2.p13.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.SS2.p13.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S3.SS2.p13.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq d\leq\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq d\leq\Delta</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="S3.Ex49" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bigl(A_{d}(\lambda)^{\frac{\Delta}{d}}+2B_{d}(\lambda)^{\frac{\Delta}{d}}\cdot x\bigr)A_{d+1}(\lambda)^{-\frac{\Delta}{d+1}}\geq A_{\Delta+1}(x)^{\frac{1}{\Delta+1}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>d</mi></mfrac></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>d</mi></mfrac></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigl(A_{d}(\lambda)^{\frac{\Delta}{d}}+2B_{d}(\lambda)^{\frac{\Delta}{d}}\cdot x\bigr)A_{d+1}(\lambda)^{-\frac{\Delta}{d+1}}\geq A_{\Delta+1}(x)^{\frac{1}{\Delta+1}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p13.3" class="ltx_p">which is shown to be true for <math id="S3.SS2.p13.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=\Delta</annotation></semantics></math> and any <math id="S3.SS2.p13.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x,\lambda\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x,\lambda\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence, if for each <math id="S3.SS2.p13.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists <math id="S3.SS2.p13.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> such that</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p14" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S3.Ex50" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bigl(A_{d}(\lambda)^{\frac{\Delta}{d}}+2B_{d}(\lambda)^{\frac{\Delta}{d}}\cdot x\bigr)A_{d+1}(\lambda)^{-\frac{\Delta}{d+1}}\geq\big(A_{\Delta}(\alpha)+2B_{\Delta}(\alpha)\cdot x\big)A_{\Delta+1}(\alpha)^{-\frac{\Delta}{\Delta+1}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>d</mi></mfrac></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>d</mi></mfrac></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigl(A_{d}(\lambda)^{\frac{\Delta}{d}}+2B_{d}(\lambda)^{\frac{\Delta}{d}}\cdot x\bigr)A_{d+1}(\lambda)^{-\frac{\Delta}{d+1}}\geq\big(A_{\Delta}(\alpha)+2B_{\Delta}(\alpha)\cdot x\big)A_{\Delta+1}(\alpha)^{-\frac{\Delta}{\Delta+1}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p14.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p14.1.1" class="ltx_text">for all <math id="S3.SS2.p14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, then we are done.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p15" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p15.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p15.1.1" class="ltx_text">To prove <math id="S3.SS2.p15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="ax+b\geq a^{\prime}x+b^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">ax+b\geq a^{\prime}x+b^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="S3.SS2.p15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, it is enough to show <math id="S3.SS2.p15.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\geq a^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>≥</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\geq a^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS2.p15.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b\geq b^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>≥</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b\geq b^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>. In our case, this means that it is enough to find <math id="S3.SS2.p15.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> such that</span></p>
<table id="S3.EGx15" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex51"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle A_{d}(\lambda)^{\frac{\Delta}{d}}A_{d+1}(\lambda)^{-\frac{\Delta}{d+1}}\geq A_{\Delta}(\alpha)A_{\Delta+1}(\alpha)^{-\frac{\Delta}{\Delta+1}}\quad\text{and}\quad B_{d}(\lambda)^{\frac{\Delta}{d}}A_{d+1}(\lambda)^{-\frac{\Delta}{d+1}}\geq B_{\Delta}(\alpha)A_{\Delta+1}(\alpha)^{-\frac{\Delta}{\Delta+1}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>d</mi></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext>and</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>d</mi></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle A_{d}(\lambda)^{\frac{\Delta}{d}}A_{d+1}(\lambda)^{-\frac{\Delta}{d+1}}\geq A_{\Delta}(\alpha)A_{\Delta+1}(\alpha)^{-\frac{\Delta}{\Delta+1}}\quad\text{and}\quad B_{d}(\lambda)^{\frac{\Delta}{d}}A_{d+1}(\lambda)^{-\frac{\Delta}{d+1}}\geq B_{\Delta}(\alpha)A_{\Delta+1}(\alpha)^{-\frac{\Delta}{\Delta+1}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p15.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p15.2.1" class="ltx_text">Rearranging these gives</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex52" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{A_{\Delta}(\alpha)^{\frac{1}{\Delta}}}{A_{\Delta+1}(\alpha)^{\frac{1}{\Delta+1}}}\leq\frac{A_{d}(\lambda)^{\frac{1}{d}}}{A_{d+1}(\lambda)^{\frac{1}{d+1}}}\quad\text{and}\quad\frac{B_{\Delta}(\alpha)^{\frac{1}{\Delta}}}{A_{\Delta+1}(\alpha)^{\frac{1}{\Delta+1}}}\leq\frac{B_{d}(\lambda)^{\frac{1}{d}}}{A_{d+1}(\lambda)^{\frac{1}{d+1}}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mfrac></msup></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>d</mi></mfrac></msup></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext>and</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mfrac></msup></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>d</mi></mfrac></msup></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{A_{\Delta}(\alpha)^{\frac{1}{\Delta}}}{A_{\Delta+1}(\alpha)^{\frac{1}{\Delta+1}}}\leq\frac{A_{d}(\lambda)^{\frac{1}{d}}}{A_{d+1}(\lambda)^{\frac{1}{d+1}}}\quad\text{and}\quad\frac{B_{\Delta}(\alpha)^{\frac{1}{\Delta}}}{A_{\Delta+1}(\alpha)^{\frac{1}{\Delta+1}}}\leq\frac{B_{d}(\lambda)^{\frac{1}{d}}}{A_{d+1}(\lambda)^{\frac{1}{d+1}}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p15.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p15.3.1" class="ltx_text">It suffices to prove the adjacent case <math id="S3.SS2.p15.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta=d+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta=d+1</annotation></semantics></math>, since iterating this comparison gives the result for arbitrary <math id="S3.SS2.p15.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\leq\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\leq\Delta</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, we want to show that there exists <math id="S3.SS2.p15.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=\alpha(\lambda,d)\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=\alpha(\lambda,d)\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> such that</span></p>
<table id="S3.E11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{A_{d+1}(\alpha)^{\frac{1}{d+1}}}{A_{d+2}(\alpha)^{\frac{1}{d+2}}}\leq\frac{A_{d}(\lambda)^{\frac{1}{d}}}{A_{d+1}(\lambda)^{\frac{1}{d+1}}}\quad\text{and}\quad\frac{B_{d+1}(\alpha)^{\frac{1}{d+1}}}{A_{d+2}(\alpha)^{\frac{1}{d+2}}}\leq\frac{B_{d}(\lambda)^{\frac{1}{d}}}{A_{d+1}(\lambda)^{\frac{1}{d+1}}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>d</mi></mfrac></msup></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext>and</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>d</mi></mfrac></msup></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{A_{d+1}(\alpha)^{\frac{1}{d+1}}}{A_{d+2}(\alpha)^{\frac{1}{d+2}}}\leq\frac{A_{d}(\lambda)^{\frac{1}{d}}}{A_{d+1}(\lambda)^{\frac{1}{d+1}}}\quad\text{and}\quad\frac{B_{d+1}(\alpha)^{\frac{1}{d+1}}}{A_{d+2}(\alpha)^{\frac{1}{d+2}}}\leq\frac{B_{d}(\lambda)^{\frac{1}{d}}}{A_{d+1}(\lambda)^{\frac{1}{d+1}}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3.11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p15.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p15.4.1" class="ltx_text">For <math id="S3.SS2.p15.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\in\{d,d+1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\in\{d,d+1\}</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="S3.SS2.p15.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{k}(x)\coloneqq A_{k}(x)/B_{k}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{k}(x)\coloneqq A_{k}(x)/B_{k}(x)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then by recalling <math id="S3.SS2.p15.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{k}(x)=k(k-1)x^{2}+2kx+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{k}(x)=k(k-1)x^{2}+2kx+1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS2.p15.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{k}(x)=kx+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{k}(x)=kx+1</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S3.E12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{k}(0)=1\quad\text{and}\quad H_{k}^{\prime}(x)=\frac{k((k-1)(kx^{2}+2x)+1)}{B_{k}(x)^{2}}&gt;0," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext>and</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{k}(0)=1\quad\text{and}\quad H_{k}^{\prime}(x)=\frac{k((k-1)(kx^{2}+2x)+1)}{B_{k}(x)^{2}}&gt;0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3.12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p15.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p15.5.1" class="ltx_text">so as a function of <math id="S3.SS2.p15.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in[0,\infty)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in[0,\infty)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.SS2.p15.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{k}(x)^{1/k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{k}(x)^{1/k}</annotation></semantics></math> is strictly increasing and <math id="S3.SS2.p15.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{k}(x)^{1/k}\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{k}(x)^{1/k}\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>. Moreover,</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex53" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex53.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{k}(x)\to\begin{cases}2&amp;if $k=1$,\\
\infty&amp;if $k\geq 2$,\end{cases}\quad\text{as }x\to\infty." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>2</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mtext>,</mtext></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mtext>,</mtext></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mtext>as </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{k}(x)\to\begin{cases}2&amp;if $k=1$,\\
\infty&amp;if $k\geq 2$,\end{cases}\quad\text{as }x\to\infty.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p15.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p15.6.1" class="ltx_text">Thus, if <math id="S3.SS2.p15.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math>, for each <math id="S3.SS2.p15.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, there is a unique <math id="S3.SS2.p15.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{k}=x_{k}(s)\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{k}=x_{k}(s)\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="S3.SS2.p15.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{k}(x_{k})^{1/k}=s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{k}(x_{k})^{1/k}=s</annotation></semantics></math>. For <math id="S3.SS2.p15.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=1</annotation></semantics></math>, a unique <math id="S3.SS2.p15.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{1}=x_{1}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1}=x_{1}(s)</annotation></semantics></math> exists such that <math id="S3.SS2.p15.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{1}(x_{1})=s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{1}(x_{1})=s</annotation></semantics></math> whenever <math id="S3.SS2.p15.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq s&lt;2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq s&lt;2</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let <math id="S3.SS2.p15.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\coloneqq H_{d}(\lambda)^{\frac{1}{d}}\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>d</mi></mfrac></msup></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\coloneqq H_{d}(\lambda)^{\frac{1}{d}}\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS2.p15.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\coloneqq x_{d+1}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\coloneqq x_{d+1}(s)</annotation></semantics></math>. Then <math id="S3.SS2.p15.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda=x_{d}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda=x_{d}(s)</annotation></semantics></math> by definition and <math id="S3.SS2.p15.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{d+1}(\alpha)^{\frac{1}{d+1}}=s=H_{d}(\lambda)^{\frac{1}{d}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>d</mi></mfrac></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{d+1}(\alpha)^{\frac{1}{d+1}}=s=H_{d}(\lambda)^{\frac{1}{d}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Note that, for <math id="S3.SS2.p15.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=1</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.SS2.p15.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{1}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1}(s)</annotation></semantics></math> is well-defined as <math id="S3.SS2.p15.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq H_{1}(\lambda)&lt;2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq H_{1}(\lambda)&lt;2</annotation></semantics></math> always.
If the second condition in (<a href="#S3.E11" title="Equation 3.11 ‣ Proof of . ‣ 3.2 Proof of ‣ 3 Semiproper colourings ‣ Lower bounds for multivariate independence polynomials and their generalisations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.11</span></a>) holds for this particular choice of <math id="S3.SS2.p15.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=\alpha(\lambda,d)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=\alpha(\lambda,d)</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e.,</span></p>
