<p id="S3.SS2.p16.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p16.2.1" class="ltx_text">To prove (<a href="#S3.E13" title="Equation 3.13 ‣ Proof of . ‣ 3.2 Proof of ‣ 3 Semiproper colourings ‣ Lower bounds for multivariate independence polynomials and their generalisations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.13</span></a>), it is enough to show <math id="S3.SS2.p16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{d+1}(s)\leq R_{d}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{d+1}(s)\leq R_{d}(s)</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="S3.SS2.p16.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>. Technically, one should assume <math id="S3.SS2.p16.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq s&lt;2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq s&lt;2</annotation></semantics></math> for the case <math id="S3.SS2.p16.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=1</annotation></semantics></math> to maintain the well-definedness of <math id="S3.SS2.p16.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{1}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1}(s)</annotation></semantics></math>, but this makes no changes in the arguments.
To this end, we compute <math id="S3.SS2.p16.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial_{s}\log R_{k}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>s</mi></msub><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial_{s}\log R_{k}(s)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Writing <math id="S3.SS2.p16.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\coloneqq x_{k}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\coloneqq x_{k}(s)</annotation></semantics></math> and using <math id="S3.SS2.p16.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{k}(x)/B_{k}(x)=s^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{k}(x)/B_{k}(x)=s^{k}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS2.p16.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{k+1}(x)=A_{k}(x)+2xB_{k}(x)=(s^{k}+2x)B_{k}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{k+1}(x)=A_{k}(x)+2xB_{k}(x)=(s^{k}+2x)B_{k}(x)</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
