<p id="S3.SS2.p16.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p16.5.1" class="ltx_text">Suppose <math id="S3.SS2.p16.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{d+1}(s)\leq sx_{d}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{d+1}(s)\leq sx_{d}(s)</annotation></semantics></math>. Then (<a href="#S3.E15" title="Equation 3.15 ‣ Proof of . ‣ 3.2 Proof of ‣ 3 Semiproper colourings ‣ Lower bounds for multivariate independence polynomials and their generalisations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.15</span></a>) implies</span></p>
