<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex59.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial_{s}\log R_{d+1}(s)\leq\partial_{s}\log R_{d}(s)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>s</mi></msub><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∂</mo><mi>s</mi></msub><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial_{s}\log R_{d+1}(s)\leq\partial_{s}\log R_{d}(s),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p16.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p16.6.1" class="ltx_text">and using <math id="S3.SS2.p16.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{d+1}(1)=R_{d}(1)=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{d+1}(1)=R_{d}(1)=1</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="S3.SS2.p16.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{d+1}(s)\leq R_{d}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{d+1}(s)\leq R_{d}(s)</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, it suffices to show <math id="S3.SS2.p16.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{d+1}(s)\leq sx_{d}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{d+1}(s)\leq sx_{d}(s)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p17" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p17.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p17.1.1" class="ltx_text">By (<a href="#S3.E12" title="Equation 3.12 ‣ Proof of . ‣ 3.2 Proof of ‣ 3 Semiproper colourings ‣ Lower bounds for multivariate independence polynomials and their generalisations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.12</span></a>), <math id="S3.SS2.p17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{d+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{d+1}</annotation></semantics></math> is strictly increasing, so <math id="S3.SS2.p17.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{d+1}(s)\leq sx_{d}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{d+1}(s)\leq sx_{d}(s)</annotation></semantics></math> is equivalent to</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex60" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex60.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s^{d+1}=H_{d+1}(x_{d+1}(s))\leq H_{d+1}(s\,x_{d}(s))." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s^{d+1}=H_{d+1}(x_{d+1}(s))\leq H_{d+1}(s\,x_{d}(s)).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p17.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p17.2.1" class="ltx_text">Write <math id="S3.SS2.p17.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\coloneqq x_{d}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\coloneqq x_{d}(s)</annotation></semantics></math>. By definition,</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex61" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex61.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{d+1}(sx)=\frac{A_{d+1}(sx)}{B_{d+1}(sx)}=1+dsx+\frac{sx}{(d+1)sx+1}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{d+1}(sx)=\frac{A_{d+1}(sx)}{B_{d+1}(sx)}=1+dsx+\frac{sx}{(d+1)sx+1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p17.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p17.3.1" class="ltx_text">On the other hand,</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex62" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex62.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s^{d+1}=s\cdot s^{d}=sH_{d}(x)=s\Bigl(1+(d-1)x+\frac{x}{dx+1}\Bigr)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s^{d+1}=s\cdot s^{d}=sH_{d}(x)=s\Bigl(1+(d-1)x+\frac{x}{dx+1}\Bigr).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p17.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p17.4.1" class="ltx_text">Recall that <math id="S3.SS2.p17.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, which implies <math id="S3.SS2.p17.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d-(d+1)s\leq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d-(d+1)s\leq 0</annotation></semantics></math>. Using this, we have</span></p>
<table id="S3.EGx17" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex63"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex63.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle H_{d+1}(sx)-s^{d+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle H_{d+1}(sx)-s^{d+1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex63.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=(1-s)+sx+sx\Bigl(\frac{1}{(d+1)sx+1}-\frac{1}{dx+1}\Bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(1-s)+sx+sx\Bigl(\frac{1}{(d+1)sx+1}-\frac{1}{dx+1}\Bigr)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex64"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex64.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=(1-s)+sx+sx\frac{(d-(d+1)s)x}{((d+1)sx+1)(dx+1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(1-s)+sx+sx\frac{(d-(d+1)s)x}{((d+1)sx+1)(dx+1)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex65"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex65.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq(1-s)+sx+sx\frac{(d-(d+1)s)x}{((d+1)s+d)x+1}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq(1-s)+sx+sx\frac{(d-(d+1)s)x}{((d+1)s+d)x+1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3.16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p17.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p17.5.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="S3.SS2.p17.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q(x)</annotation></semantics></math> be the expression obtained by multiplying (<a href="#S3.Ex65" title="Equation 3.16 ‣ Proof of . ‣ 3.2 Proof of ‣ 3 Semiproper colourings ‣ Lower bounds for multivariate independence polynomials and their generalisations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.16</span></a>) by <math id="S3.SS2.p17.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="((d+1)s+d)x+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">((d+1)s+d)x+1</annotation></semantics></math>. Then</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex66" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex66.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q(x)=(1-s)\big(((d+1)s+d)x+1\big)+sx(2dx+1)=2dsx^{2}+(2s+d-s^{2}d-s^{2})x-(s-1)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q(x)=(1-s)\big(((d+1)s+d)x+1\big)+sx(2dx+1)=2dsx^{2}+(2s+d-s^{2}d-s^{2})x-(s-1).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p17.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p17.6.1" class="ltx_text">As <math id="S3.SS2.p17.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2ds&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2ds&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.SS2.p17.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q(0)\leq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q(0)\leq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S3.SS2.p17.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q(s-1)=(d-1)(s-1)^{3}\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q(s-1)=(d-1)(s-1)^{3}\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, this quadratic polynomial <math id="S3.SS2.p17.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q(x)</annotation></semantics></math> is nonnegative on <math id="S3.SS2.p17.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\geq s-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\geq s-1</annotation></semantics></math>. Indeed, <math id="S3.SS2.p17.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=x_{d}(s)\geq s-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=x_{d}(s)\geq s-1</annotation></semantics></math>, as</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex67" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex67.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1+d(s-1)\leq s^{d}=H_{d}(x)=1+(d-1)x+\frac{x}{dx+1}\leq 1+dx." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1+d(s-1)\leq s^{d}=H_{d}(x)=1+(d-1)x+\frac{x}{dx+1}\leq 1+dx.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p17.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p17.7.1" class="ltx_text">Hence, <math id="S3.SS2.p17.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{d+1}(sx)\geq s^{d+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{d+1}(sx)\geq s^{d+1}</annotation></semantics></math>, which concludes the proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmremarkx2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmremarkx2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Remark</span></span><span id="Thmremarkx2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmremarkx2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmremarkx2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">While <em id="Thmremarkx2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Aletheia</em>’s output was closer to an incomplete proof sketch than a complete proof, it contained several significant ideas. For instance, it suggested using the dual set <math id="Thmremarkx2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> and its log-convexity; it also provided a preliminary form of <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem5" title="Lemma 3.5. ‣ 3.2 Proof of ‣ 3 Semiproper colourings ‣ Lower bounds for multivariate independence polynomials and their generalisations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.5</span></a> and the reduction technique for <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma 3.3. ‣ 3.1 The dual set 𝒮_𝑑 and log-convexity ‣ 3 Semiproper colourings ‣ Lower bounds for multivariate independence polynomials and their generalisations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a>. Based on these insights, we formalised the arguments and filled in the necessary details. In particular, for <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem4" title="Lemma 3.4. ‣ 3.1 The dual set 𝒮_𝑑 and log-convexity ‣ 3 Semiproper colourings ‣ Lower bounds for multivariate independence polynomials and their generalisations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.4</span></a> and the symmetric case of <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma 3.3. ‣ 3.1 The dual set 𝒮_𝑑 and log-convexity ‣ 3 Semiproper colourings ‣ Lower bounds for multivariate independence polynomials and their generalisations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a>, we retained only the statements provided by the model and wrote the proofs entirely independently, using different methods to ensure clarity and simplicity.</p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S4" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">4 </span>More towards <a href="#S1.Thmtheorem3" title="Conjecture 1.3. ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ Lower bounds for multivariate independence polynomials and their generalisations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Conjecture</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.3</span></a></h2>

<div id="S4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Recall that <a href="#S1.Thmtheorem3" title="Conjecture 1.3. ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ Lower bounds for multivariate independence polynomials and their generalisations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Conjecture</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.3</span></a> states that for any graph <math id="S4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> and antiferromagnetic edge-weighted graph <math id="S4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="S4.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hom(G,H)\geq\prod_{v\in V(G)}\hom(K_{d_{v}+1},H)^{\frac{1}{d_{v}+1}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>hom</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≥</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>hom</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hom(G,H)\geq\prod_{v\in V(G)}\hom(K_{d_{v}+1},H)^{\frac{1}{d_{v}+1}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4.1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">We show that this holds if <math id="S4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta(G)\leq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta(G)\leq 2</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 4.1</span></span><span id="S4.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><a href="#S1.Thmtheorem3" title="Conjecture 1.3. ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ Lower bounds for multivariate independence polynomials and their generalisations" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Conjecture</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.3</span></a><span id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is true if <math id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta(G)\leq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta(G)\leq 2</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Since both sides of (<a href="#S4.E1" title="Equation 4.1 ‣ 4 More towards ‣ Lower bounds for multivariate independence polynomials and their generalisations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>) are multiplicative over the connected components of <math id="S4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>, it suffices to consider the case when <math id="S4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> is connected. Thus, we assume <math id="S4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> is either a path or a cycle.
Let <math id="S4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{1}\geq\mu_{2}\geq\dots\geq\mu_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≥</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">⋯</mi><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{1}\geq\mu_{2}\geq\dots\geq\mu_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> be the spectrum of <math id="S4.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Suppose first that <math id="S4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> is an <math id="S4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math>-edge path <math id="S4.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S4.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>.
By a classical result of Cvetković, Doob, and Sachs <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">4</a>, Theorem 1.10]</cite> (also see <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">5</a>, Theorem 1.3.5]</cite> for a recent source), there exist nonnegative reals <math id="S4.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{1},\dots,p_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{1},\dots,p_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i=1}^{n}p_{i}=n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i=1}^{n}p_{i}=n</annotation></semantics></math>, such that the (weighted) number of <math id="S4.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>-edge walks in <math id="S4.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S4.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{1}\mu_{1}^{m}+\cdots+p_{n}\mu_{n}^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>m</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>m</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{1}\mu_{1}^{m}+\cdots+p_{n}\mu_{n}^{m}</annotation></semantics></math> for each <math id="S4.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>. We then have, by using the antiferromagnetism condition <math id="S4.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{i}\leq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{i}\leq 0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lvert\mu_{i}\rvert\leq\mu_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lvert\mu_{i}\rvert\leq\mu_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> for each <math id="S4.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx18" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hom(P_{\ell},H)=p_{1}\mu_{1}^{\ell}+\dots+p_{n}\mu_{n}^{\ell}\geq\mu_{1}^{\ell-1}(p_{1}\mu_{1}+\cdots+p_{n}\mu_{n})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>hom</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">⋯</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>n</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hom(P_{\ell},H)=p_{1}\mu_{1}^{\ell}+\dots+p_{n}\mu_{n}^{\ell}\geq\mu_{1}^{\ell-1}(p_{1}\mu_{1}+\cdots+p_{n}\mu_{n}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">Again by antiferromagnetism, <math id="S4.p3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{1}^{3}\geq\mu_{1}^{3}+\dots+\mu_{n}^{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></msubsup><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">⋯</mi><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>n</mi><mn>3</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{1}^{3}\geq\mu_{1}^{3}+\dots+\mu_{n}^{3}</annotation></semantics></math>, so</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx19" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mu_{1}^{\ell-1}(p_{1}\mu_{1}+\cdots+p_{n}\mu_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mu_{1}^{\ell-1}(p_{1}\mu_{1}+\cdots+p_{n}\mu_{n})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq(\mu_{1}^{3}+\cdots+\mu_{n}^{3})^{\frac{\ell-1}{3}}(p_{1}\mu_{1}+\cdots+p_{n}\mu_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>n</mi><mn>3</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq(\mu_{1}^{3}+\cdots+\mu_{n}^{3})^{\frac{\ell-1}{3}}(p_{1}\mu_{1}+\cdots+p_{n}\mu_{n})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\hom(K_{3},H)^{\frac{\ell-1}{3}}\hom(K_{2},H)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>hom</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>hom</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\hom(K_{3},H)^{\frac{\ell-1}{3}}\hom(K_{2},H),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">which is the desired bound.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Suppose now that <math id="S4.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> is a copy of <math id="S4.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math>, the cycle of length <math id="S4.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell\geq 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell\geq 3</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, by using <math id="S4.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lvert\mu_{i}\rvert\leq\mu_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lvert\mu_{i}\rvert\leq\mu_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> for each <math id="S4.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx20" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hom(C_{\ell},H)=\mu_{1}^{\ell}+\cdots+\mu_{n}^{\ell}\geq\mu_{1}^{\ell-3}(\mu_{1}^{3}+\cdots+\mu_{n}^{3})\geq(\mu_{1}^{3}+\cdots+\mu_{n}^{3})^{\frac{\ell}{3}}=\hom(K_{3},H)^{\frac{\ell}{3}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>hom</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>n</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>n</mi><mn>3</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>n</mi><mn>3</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>3</mn></mfrac></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>hom</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>3</mn></mfrac></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hom(C_{\ell},H)=\mu_{1}^{\ell}+\cdots+\mu_{n}^{\ell}\geq\mu_{1}^{\ell-3}(\mu_{1}^{3}+\cdots+\mu_{n}^{3})\geq(\mu_{1}^{3}+\cdots+\mu_{n}^{3})^{\frac{\ell}{3}}=\hom(K_{3},H)^{\frac{\ell}{3}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the last inequality uses <math id="S4.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{1}^{3}\geq\mu_{1}^{3}+\cdots+\mu_{n}^{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></msubsup><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>n</mi><mn>3</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{1}^{3}\geq\mu_{1}^{3}+\cdots+\mu_{n}^{3}</annotation></semantics></math>. This concludes the proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
