<p id="S4.p9.4" class="ltx_p">If <math id="S4.p9.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda^{(1)},\lambda^{(2)}=o(1/\Delta(G))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda^{(1)},\lambda^{(2)}=o(1/\Delta(G))</annotation></semantics></math>, the factors in this lower bound for <math id="S4.p9.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{G}^{(2)}(\lambda^{(1)},\lambda^{(2)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mi>G</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{G}^{(2)}(\lambda^{(1)},\lambda^{(2)})</annotation></semantics></math> match the conjectured factors of <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem2" title="Conjecture 4.2. ‣ 4 More towards ‣ Lower bounds for multivariate independence polynomials and their generalisations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Conjecture</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a> up to the linear terms. Indeed, as <math id="S4.p9.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta(G)\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta(G)\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
