<p id="S5.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">If <math id="S5.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\lambda}=(1,\dots,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝝀</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\lambda}=(1,\dots,1)</annotation></semantics></math>, this is exactly <math id="S5.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{G}(\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{G}(\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math>. Then <a href="#S1.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1.1. ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ Lower bounds for multivariate independence polynomials and their generalisations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.1</span></a> follows by showing</p>
<table id="S5.E2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{G}(t;\bm{\lambda})\geq\frac{1}{\lvert V(G)\rvert}\sum_{v\in V(G)}\alpha_{K_{d_{v}+1}}(t\lambda_{v}),\qquad t\in\mathbb{R}_{\geq 0},\,\bm{\lambda}\in(\mathbb{R}_{\geq 0})^{V(G)}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝝀</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>v</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mi>𝝀</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{G}(t;\bm{\lambda})\geq\frac{1}{\lvert V(G)\rvert}\sum_{v\in V(G)}\alpha_{K_{d_{v}+1}}(t\lambda_{v}),\qquad t\in\mathbb{R}_{\geq 0},\,\bm{\lambda}\in(\mathbb{R}_{\geq 0})^{V(G)},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5.2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.3" class="ltx_p">multiplying both sides by <math id="S5.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lvert V(G)\rvert/t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lvert V(G)\rvert/t</annotation></semantics></math>, and integrating with respect to <math id="S5.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> over <math id="S5.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>. Putting <math id="S5.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\lambda}=(1,\dots,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝝀</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\lambda}=(1,\dots,1)</annotation></semantics></math>, we see that (<a href="#S5.E1" title="Equation 5.1 ‣ Occupancy fractions ‣ 5 Concluding remarks ‣ Lower bounds for multivariate independence polynomials and their generalisations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.1</span></a>) is a special case of (<a href="#S5.E2" title="Equation 5.2 ‣ Occupancy fractions ‣ 5 Concluding remarks ‣ Lower bounds for multivariate independence polynomials and their generalisations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.2</span></a>). Moreover, (<a href="#S5.E2" title="Equation 5.2 ‣ Occupancy fractions ‣ 5 Concluding remarks ‣ Lower bounds for multivariate independence polynomials and their generalisations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.2</span></a>) is equivalent to showing that for all <math id="S5.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\lambda}\in(\mathbb{R}_{\geq 0})^{V(G)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝝀</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\lambda}\in(\mathbb{R}_{\geq 0})^{V(G)}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
